hint.duck=The wild ducks overhead only come down to stay where there is water, with lily pads and reeds close by.
hint.duck.rare=No one has seen a rare duck yet. Keep your pond lovely and see.
hint.camel=A camel wanders in when there is warm sand, a few cacti and plenty of open room.
hint.goat=A goat bounds over to rocks it can climb and leafy things to nibble.
hint.camel.rare=A moonlit camel, pale as the dunes at night, visits shelters with cacti where two or more camels are truly content.
hint.goat.rare=A slate goat is drawn to a shed with plenty of rocks and leafy things, where everything a goat could wish for is close by.
role.camel_moonlit=Moonlit Camel
role.goat_slate=Slate Goat
rare.camel=Moonlit Camel
rare.goat=Slate Goat
hint.rabbit=Wild rabbits come by a hutch on open grass, most of all when carrots or lettuce grow nearby.
hint.mouse=Mice sneak up to a cottage with a pile of hay close by, and a field of grain makes them bolder.
hint.rabbit.rare=A rabbit as white as snow has been seen near hutches where carrots and flowers grow and two rabbits already live.
hint.mouse.rare=A golden mouse is said to visit cottages beside a grain field, but only when a few seed pouches are waiting inside.
role.rabbit_snow=Snowy Rabbit
role.mouse_golden=Golden Mouse
rare.rabbit=Snowy Rabbit
rare.mouse=Golden Mouse
hint.squirrel=Squirrels scamper over to houses near trees, with some shade and flowers.
hint.crab=Crabs scuttle up from the water to sandy shores with seaweed and shells.
hint.mosshorn=Mosshorns amble out of the woods toward shade, mossy ground, ferns and a few mushrooms under the trees.
hint.mosshorn.rare=Nobody has yet seen a mosshorn rarer than the rest.
hint.turkey=Turkeys strut over to open grass with a fence or log to perch on and a trough of corn.
hint.turkey.rare=Nobody has yet seen a turkey rarer than the rest.
hint.tortoise=A tortoise plods over to a burrow out in the open sun, most of all when lettuce or flowers grow close by.
hint.meerkat=Meerkats scamper up to a mound on warm sand, and a fence post to keep watch from makes them stay.
hint.fox=Foxes never wander in on their own. Set out a Bait Bowl with raw chicken or fish nearby and keep still.
hint.wolf=Wolves keep away from houses. Fill a Bait Bowl with raw meat where a pack roams, then wait for them to calm down.
hint.bear=Bears never wander in by themselves. Find one in the woods and set out a Bait Bowl with fish or berries.
hint.bear.rare=Nobody has yet seen a bear rarer than the rest.
hint.snowleopard=Snow leopards never come down on their own. Find one in the snowy peaks and set out a Bait Bowl with raw meat or fish.
hint.snowleopard.rare=Nobody has yet seen a snow leopard rarer than the rest.
hint.deer=A deer steps out of the trees where the woods meet a quiet meadow, with long grass to hide in.
hint.deer.rare=No one has seen a rare deer yet. Keep your shelter quiet and lovely and see.
hint.bison=Bison drift in from the plains where there is wide open grass and hay to share.
hint.bison.rare=No one has seen a rare bison yet. Keep your herd happy and see.
hint.warthog=A warthog trots in, tail up, wherever there is bare dry earth to dig and a bit of mud to roll in.
hint.warthog.rare=No one has seen a rare warthog yet. Keep your wallow muddy and see.
hint.antelope=Antelope wander in from wide open grassland, but only where it is quiet and there is plenty of room to run.
hint.antelope.rare=No one has seen a rare antelope yet. Keep your herd calm and see.
